cla_mmrs: describe CLA lane selects, match events and SMC-inactive controls

Several CLA MMR descriptions disagreed with the RTL:

- The debug-bus mux lane selects read as one-hot ("if bit[0] = 1 ... Seg4,
  if bit[1] = 1 ... Seg5"), but each select is a binary index: 0 picks the
  lane's static segment and k picks segment (output lanes + k - 1), so 4
  selects Seg7. The fields now give the valid range for the SMC CLA mux
  (four 16-bit output lanes from 16 input segments, plus the fine-grain
  time slot) and mark the selects the four-lane mux never reads.
- Mask/match set 3 claimed event 0x1D, which is set 2's negative event.
  Each set produces a positive then a negative event from 0x2 and 0x1C,
  so set 3 is 0x1E/0x1F. All four sets now name both events.
- ClaChainLoopDelay described a window that also suppressed clock halt.
  The self filter masks the matching incoming cross-trigger for one cycle,
  ClaChainLoopDelay cycles after the CLA's own cross-trigger action, and
  never touches clock halt.
- Snapshot descriptions for Node1 Eap1, Node2 Eap0/1 and Node3 Eap0/1
  named the wrong node or EAP.

The SMC instantiates the CLA with a 64-bit debug bus and local timestamp
scheme 0, so the Hi halves of the event configuration and snapshot
registers, CDbgMuxSelHi, ts_capture, CDbgTimestampCapture and
CDbgClaTimestampOffset have no effect there; their descriptions now say so.

Recorded as a patch so the hand-mirrored upstream/ tree stays
reproducible from the vendored spec plus patches/ applied in order.
